  "title": "Make Sure You Catch The Debut Of People Talking Sports After Cavs & Knicks Game",
  "htmlContent": "[caption id=\"attachment_502566\" align=\"aligncenter\" width=\"479\"]<img class=\"size-full wp-image-502566\" src=\"http://35.224.26.164/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/52024265_336542230307194_2076985549055165240_n.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"479\" height=\"359\"> Courtesy of Brandon Robinson[/caption]\n\nHeavy Contributor and Basketball Society's Senior Editor&nbsp; Brandon “Scoop B“ Robinson will be featured on a show that will be making its debut on MSG Network entitled People Talking Sports. His Co-hosts are Bryan Fonesca of Nets Daily, Fox New York's Jennifer Williams, and Bleacher Reports Fernando Perez.\n\nThe show is a reboot of that originally made its debut back in 2017, featuring Sam Morril and Liz Gonzales.&nbsp; Kia Motors USA will be sponsoring the reboot. The concept of the show would be four people in a Kia in New York City talking&nbsp; NY Sports.\n\nEarlier today Robinson posted a clip of the cast in A Kia via his Instagram account.\n<blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" style=\"background: #FFF; border: 0; border-radius: 3px; box-shadow: 0 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.5),0 1px 10px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.15); margin: 1px; max-width: 540px; min-width: 326px; padding: 0; width: calc(100% - 2px);\" data-instgrm-captioned=\"\" data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/BucYBwlDECc/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_medium=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"12\">\n<div style=\"padding: 16px;\">\n<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: center;\">\n<div style=\"background-color: #f4f4f4; border-radius: 50%; flex-grow: 0; height: 40px; margin-right: 14px; width: 40px;\"></div>\n<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex-grow: 1; justify-content: center;\">\n<div style=\"background-color: #f4f4f4; border-radius: 4px; flex-grow: 0; height: 14px; margin-bottom: 6px; width: 100px;\"></div>\n<div style=\"background-color: #f4f4f4; border-radius: 4px; flex-grow: 0; height: 14px; width: 60px;\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"padding: 19% 0;\"></div>\n<div style=\"display: block; height: 50px; margin: 0 auto 12px; width: 50px;\"></div>\n<div style=\"padding-top: 8px;\">\n<div style=\"color: #3897f0; font-family: Arial,sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 550; line-height: 18px;\">View this post on Instagram</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"padding: 12.5% 0;\"></div>\n<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; margin-bottom: 14px; align-items: center;\">\n<div>\n<div style=\"background-color: #f4f4f4; border-radius: 50%; height: 12.5px; width: 12.5px; transform: translateX(0px) translateY(7px);\"></div>\n<div style=\"background-color: #f4f4f4; height: 12.5px; transform: rotate(-45deg) translateX(3px) translateY(1px); width: 12.5px; flex-grow: 0; margin-right: 14px; margin-left: 2px;\"></div>\n<div style=\"background-color: #f4f4f4; border-radius: 50%; height: 12.5px; width: 12.5px; transform: translateX(9px) translateY(-18px);\"></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"margin-left: 8px;\">\n<div style=\"background-color: #f4f4f4; border-radius: 50%; flex-grow: 0; height: 20px; width: 20px;\"></div>\n<div style=\"width: 0; height: 0; border-top: 2px solid transparent; border-left: 6px solid #f4f4f4; border-bottom: 2px solid transparent; transform: translateX(16px) translateY(-4px) rotate(30deg);\"></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"margin-left: auto;\">\n<div style=\"width: 0px; border-top: 8px solid #F4F4F4; border-right: 8px solid transparent; transform: translateY(16px);\"></div>\n<div style=\"background-color: #f4f4f4; flex-grow: 0; height: 12px; width: 16px; transform: translateY(-4px);\"></div>\n<div style=\"width: 0; height: 0; border-top: 8px solid #F4F4F4; border-left: 8px solid transparent; transform: translateY(-4px) translateX(8px);\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p style=\"margin: 8px 0 0 0; padding: 0 4px;\"><a style=\"color: #000; font-family: Arial,sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: 17px; text-decoration: none; word-wrap: break-word;\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/BucYBwlDECc/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_medium=loading\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TONIGHT IS THE NIGHT! MSG Networks’ People Talking Sports will air its rebooted debut episode tonight following the New York Knicks postgame show. ☝️ Link In Bio ☝️ Excited for you to see what @jenxperience @bryanfonsecany @ifernandoperez3 and I are working on! You can watch tonight around 10:30 PM TONIGHT on MSG Network. If you’re not in New York, New Jersey and Connecticut, no problem! Google: Reddit NBA Live stream app. Look for: Cleveland Cavaliers/ New York Knicks game on MSG Network. The show will be on after the post game show of Knicks/Cavaliers on MSG Network</a></p>\n<p style=\"color: #c9c8cd; font-family: Arial,sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 17px; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 8px; overflow: hidden; padding: 8px 0 7px; text-align: center; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap;\">A post shared by <a style=\"color: #c9c8cd; font-family: Arial,sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: 17px;\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/scoop_b/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_medium=loading\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">   Brandon 'Scoop B' Robinson</a> (@scoop_b) on <time style=\"font-family: Arial,sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 17px;\" datetime=\"2019-02-28T23:10:57+00:00\">Feb 28, 2019 at 3:10pm PST</time></p>\n\n</div></blockquote>\n<script async=\"\" src=\"//www.instagram.com/embed.js\"></script>\n\nRobinson sent an email to <a href=\"https://nothinbutnets.com/2019/02/28/brooklyn-nets-familiar-faces-debut-new-show-msg-thursday-night/?fbclid=IwAR0pQHHwtocbTmRBcrBNXvz6ocXnLlRjZB7qvz6QlQCxsG7X8vZzPMJpp0Q\">Notinbutnets.com's Phil Watson</a> sharing some details about the 30-minute program.\n\n“We’ve been working on this project and concept since December — taping, meeting, auditions … and now it’s here,“ said Robinson.\n\nThe show will premiere after tonight's game between the Knicks and the Cavaliers On MSG Network.",
